  "description": "NEW TO THE MARKET\n\nCARN BEG, AGHAMORE,\nBALLYHAUNIS, CO. MAYO\nF35 AE78\n\nFOLIO: MY39518\n\n2 BEDROOM DETACHED BUNGALOW\nON c.1 ACRE\n\nASKING PRICE: €150,000\n\nHABITABLE RESIDENCE WITH EXCELLENT REFURBISHMENT POTENTIAL\n\n\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers are delighted to bring to the market this attractive two-bedroom detached bungalow at Carn Beg, Aghamore, Ballyhaunis, Co. Mayo.\n\nSet on approximately 1 acre, this traditional country residence is presented in good, habitable condition and offers an excellent opportunity for a purchaser looking for a home which can be occupied while being modernised and upgraded over time.\n\nThe property is in good structural condition and benefits from PVC windows and doors, mains water, electricity and its own septic tank.\n\nWhile perfectly liveable in its present condition, the residence offers considerable potential for refurbishment and upgrading to create a very attractive modern country home.\n\nThe property may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to the purchaser and property satisfying the relevant scheme requirements.\n\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nThe accommodation is conveniently arranged on one level and comprises:\n\nKitchen / Dining Room\n\nLiving Room\n\nBack Kitchen\n\nBedroom 1\n\nBedroom 2\n\nBathroom\n\n\nOUTSIDE\n\nThe residence is being offered on approximately 1 acre, providing generous outdoor space around the property.\n\nThe grounds offer excellent potential for a purchaser to further landscape and develop the property to suit their own requirements.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nCarn Beg enjoys an attractive rural setting just off the main Ballyhaunis to Tooreen road in a well-established residential and agricultural area.\n\nThe property combines the benefits of peaceful countryside living with convenient access to Ballyhaunis, Aghamore, Tooreen and the surrounding areas.\n\n\nGENERAL FEATURES\n\n2 bedroom detached bungalow\n\nSet on approximately 1 acre\n\nHabitable residence\n\nGood structural condition\n\nExcellent refurbishment and modernisation potential\n\nMay qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to scheme criteria\n\nPVC windows and doors\n\nMains water\n\nElectricity connected\n\nSeptic tank\n\nAttractive countryside setting\n\nConvenient to the Ballyhaunis–Tooreen road\n\nEircode: F35 AE78\n\n\nVIEWING\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity to acquire a habitable detached country residence on a generous site at an attractive price point.\n\nThe combination of its c.1 acre setting, existing services and potential for further refurbishment makes this a property well worth viewing.\n\nViewing comes highly recommended and is strictly by appointment with the Sole Selling Agents.\n\nFor further particulars or to arrange a viewing, contact:\n\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers\n\nNigel: 086 213 0723\n\nOffice: 094 936 2216\n\n\nEverything we touch turns to SOLD.\n\n\nSOLE SELLING AGENT\n\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers\n\n\nDISCLAIMER\n\nThese particulars, including site area, measurements, distances, services and descriptions, are provided for guidance purposes only and do not form part of any contract. The agents have not tested any services, appliances or equipment. Intending purchasers should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy of all information provided. Any grant availability or eligibility is subject to the property and applicant satisfying the relevant scheme criteria and obtaining all necessary approvals.",
